WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.149
Your forecast is off by forty percent... but do you know where it misses?

00:00:05.410 --> 00:00:08.156
Every demand review has the same argument.

00:00:08.348 --> 00:00:10.666
Planning blames sales.

00:00:10.716 --> 00:00:12.858
Sales blames the market.

00:00:12.992 --> 00:00:14.774
And nobody brings a number.

00:00:14.907 --> 00:00:17.363
The first step is to break the error down.

00:00:17.716 --> 00:00:19.464
Don't look only at the total.

00:00:19.539 --> 00:00:21.577
Look by product family.

00:00:21.931 --> 00:00:25.652
Almost always, a few items explain most of the error.

00:00:25.843 --> 00:00:31.248
Then compare the statistical forecast with the forecast adjusted by sales.

00:00:31.439 --> 00:00:36.219
If the adjustment makes the result worse... the problem is not the model.

00:00:36.294 --> 00:00:40.656
That is called FVA: Forecast Value Add.

00:00:40.706 --> 00:00:41.910
And check the bias.

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:47.901
If the error always goes the same way, you end up with too much or too little stock every month.

00:00:47.951 --> 00:00:49.187
That is bias.

00:00:49.541 --> 00:00:54.472
With these three cuts, the meeting stops being about blame and becomes about action.

00:00:54.522 --> 00:00:57.465
Comment FORECAST and I will send you the checklist.
